cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BharatBench, please cite it as below. Code is MIT-licensed; the dataset is CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA)."
title: "BharatBench: a benchmark of how well LLMs handle real Indian tasks"
type: dataset
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adityajamdhade6/bharatbench"
url: "https://bharatbench.vercel.app/"
abstract: >-
  BharatBench measures how well large language models handle real Indian tasks:
  GST and tax math, Hinglish and Hindi customer support, extraction from Indian
  documents, Indian law and policy, and payments and banking support. Every
  task has a worked solution or an official source, and all documents are
  synthetic. A private held-out set guards against training on the answers.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - India
  - Hinglish
  - evaluation
authors:
  - family-names: "Jamdhade"
    given-names: "Aditya"
